{
  "__readme": [
    "Shared ground truth for the two hand-mirrored harness MCP proxy token",
    "verifiers: the inspector's PRODUCTION verifier",
    "(mcpjam-inspector/server/utils/harness/harness-proxy-token.ts) and the",
    "backend's parity verifier (convex/lib/harnessMcpProxyToken.ts). Neither can",
    "import the other, so each side runs its own verifier against THESE BYTES.",
    "",
    "The two copies are BYTE-IDENTICAL by design \u2014 this file is pinned whole in",
    "convex/lib/mirrors.json, so `check:mirrors --upstream` compares them",
    "directly and any drift is real drift rather than a wording difference.",
    "Copies live at tests/convex/fixtures/ (backend) and",
    "server/utils/harness/__tests__/fixtures/ (inspector).",
    "",
    "The tokens are signed with `secret` below \u2014 a fixture-only value, never a",
    "deployment secret. `nowSeconds`/`expSeconds` fix the clock so the expiry",
    "boundary is testable exactly: a token is expired AT exp, not after it, and",
    "both verifiers must agree on that single second. They did not before",
    "2026-08-31: the backend used `>` and accepted a token for the whole second",
    "it expired in while the inspector used `>=` and rejected it \u2014 a token the",
    "control plane calls valid and the data plane refuses, which presents as",
    "'the harness randomly loses its tools'.",
    "",
    "The eval-scope claims (runId/iterationId) travel TOGETHER or not at all.",
    "The `halfPair*` vectors are FORGED \u2014 validly signed, but carrying one of",
    "the pair \u2014 because no minter produces that shape; they exist so both",
    "verifiers prove they drop a half-present scope rather than surfacing an",
    "iteration claim nothing authorized."
  ],
